hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-13 = cons "*Navigate* is *navis* + *agere*, driving a ship, and *govern* comes from Greek *kybernan*, to steer, which also gives *cybernetics*. Steering and governing were the same word in Greek. Navigating information space is self-government in the oldest sense: steering your own ship. That's why complete user agency over the endpoint isn't a feature request; it's the meaning of navigation. A person who doesn't steer isn't navigating, they're being carried." (cons "" nil)
